body.p:
The Claims also recite: upon the user beginning the second session, prompt the user for their level of mental fatigue at the end of the first session. This is also not present in Alcaide. This user in Alcaide is provided with directives to take a break due to detected fatigue, but the user in Alcaide is never prompted for their level of mental fatigue. See Alcaide,   0039. Importantly, the Claims do not just recite prompting the user for their current level of mental fatigue. Instead, the Claims prompt the user for their level of mental fatigue at the end of the prior session of operation of the IHS. As inventors have recognized, this retrospective evaluation of fatigue provides more reliable data and this specific prompting is thus incorporated into theIHS detecting the user has resumed operation of the IHS after a break. See e.g., Specification SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.150.2270050. The user is not prompted in Alcaide, and there is certainly no teaching or suggestion in Alcaide of any such prompting for retroactive evaluation of fatigue.
